From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: free the encoder instance slot when the
 component is released

V4L2EncodeComponent counts its instances and refuses to create more than
ro.vendor.v4l2_codec2.encode_concurrent_instances. MediaCodec turns the
refusal (NO_MEMORY) into a request to the resource manager to reclaim a
hardware codec from a lower-priority client, then retries the
allocation. The count only dropped in the destructor, but the Codec2 HAL
keeps the component object until the client lets go of its last
reference, and CCodec drops that reference in a message it posts after
the release has completed. The reclaimed component can therefore still
be alive when MediaCodec retries right after the reclaim returned. The
retry then fails although the hardware encoder is free, and after two
reclaims the client falls back to a software encoder, or fails to start
where there is none.

Drop the count in release() as well, once per component. release()
stops the component, which destroys the V4L2 encoder on the encoder
thread before it returns. That closes the device, and with it the driver
session, as nothing else holds the device file: both queues use DMABUF
memory, so nothing is mapped, and the poll thread has been stopped. A
released component cannot be started again. The count is still taken
when the component is created, so the limit keeps showing up as
NO_MEMORY at create time, which is what reclaim and fallback rely on.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.cpp                  | 20 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.h    |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.cpp b/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.cpp
index 07a6f63..e58f813 100644
--- a/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.cpp
+++ b/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.cpp
@@ -52,7 +52,25 @@ V4L2EncodeComponent::V4L2EncodeComponent(C2String name, c2_node_id_t id,
 
 V4L2EncodeComponent::~V4L2EncodeComponent() {
     ALOGV("%s():", __func__);
-    sConcurrentInstances.fetch_sub(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    releaseInstance();
+}
+
+c2_status_t V4L2EncodeComponent::release() {
+    ALOGV("%s()", __func__);
+
+    // Releasing stops the component, which destroys the V4L2 encoder and closes the device, so the
+    // hardware encoder is free again when this returns. The client may keep the released component
+    // alive for a while: a codec reclaimed by the resource manager is only destroyed after the
+    // reclaim returned, and the new client retries at once. Leave room for it now.
+    c2_status_t status = EncodeComponent::release();
+    releaseInstance();
+    return status;
+}
+
+void V4L2EncodeComponent::releaseInstance() {
+    if (!mInstanceReleased.exchange(true)) {
+        sConcurrentInstances.fetch_sub(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
 }
 
 bool V4L2EncodeComponent::initializeEncoder() {
diff --git a/v4l2/include/v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.h b/v4l2/include/v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.h
index 79d99d0..e2f3edc 100644
--- a/v4l2/include/v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.h
+++ b/v4l2/include/v4l2_codec2/v4l2/V4L2EncodeComponent.h
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ public:
 
     virtual ~V4L2EncodeComponent() override;
 
+    c2_status_t release() override;
+
 protected:
     bool initializeEncoder() override;
 
@@ -26,6 +28,12 @@ private:
     static std::atomic<int32_t> sConcurrentInstances;
 
     V4L2EncodeComponent(C2String name, c2_node_id_t id, std::shared_ptr<EncodeInterface> interface);
+
+    // Stop counting this component as a concurrent instance, if not done yet.
+    void releaseInstance();
+
+    // Whether this component no longer counts as a concurrent instance.
+    std::atomic<bool> mInstanceReleased{false};
 };
 
 }  // namespace android
